% review-id: mikhahi-labu
% review-from: holding
% review-status: change
% review-categories: sexual, substances, context
% review-findings: Verse 1, line 2: "sarat havu biaram?" (shall I bring a second wife over your head?). Verse 2: "qeri-to doshak biaram?", Strettell: "A new mattress by thine to-night?" (bedroom innuendo). Verses 3 and 4: cigarettes ("sigar"). The refrain "na-na-i" is clean. The dossier wrongly says verses 2 to 4 are fine.
% review-suggestion: Correct the dossier first. For class, sing only the first line ("mikhahi labu biaram?", shall I bring you hot beetroot?) with the refrain, or choose another of Fairchild's twelve songs after reading its words.
% review-decision: published to main on 11 November 2026 with the first line sung twice and the refrain (bar 3 sung to bar 1's words, without the slur on its first two notes); left out: verse 1 line 2 (the second-wife joke), verse 2 (the mattress line) and verses 3 and 4 (cigarettes); no %%tuning (Fairchild prints F natural; a koron F is a question for a Persian musician); dossier-respect corrected as the review asked; keep correcting here
